G1 a kernel writing into a Mut<Float32Array> parameter (MUTARG with a Mut-typed argument)
   fill: ok
   filled: ok
G2 reduce with an accumulator mutated in the callback (MUTARG)
   evens: rejected [mutating-method] L2 write to a number[], which is not Mut
G2b the same as filter
   evens: ok
G3 new Date(t).toISOString() (DATE)
   stamp: rejected [new-non-intrinsic] L2 new on something that is not an allowed intrinsic
G4 an htl view inside the JSX vocabulary, with a click handler (Y by tag scan)
   count: ok
   inc: ok
   view: ok
G5 an htl view with <a href> and <table> (JSX by tag scan)
   view: rejected [no-member] L2 <a> is not a declared element; [no-member] L2 <table> is not a declared element
G6 width taken as an outside number (BUILTIN: whether the runtime resolves it is not a checker question)
   half: ok
G7 Object.assign onto a fresh literal, and .catch on a promise (unsupported-method list)
   merged: unsupported
   safe: unsupported
G8 for..of over an array of records, === between records (strict-eq-object, which classify.ts cannot see)
   findIndex: rejected [strict-eq-object] L2 === on two non-primitive operands; use equals(a, b)
